From 4c699eb4a554821befef0b5a96ba1caee049ce1b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Julius Bairaktaris <julius@bairaktaris.de>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 00:03:48 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] sha512: keep the target CPU when enabling the SHA-3
 extensions

On AArch64, "arch=armv8.2-a+sha3" replaces the -mcpu/-march of the
build with plain Armv8.2-A. For a CPU with more extensions, such as
-mcpu=cortex-a76, GCC then refuses to inline always_inline functions
compiled for the full target, such as a fortified memset().

Use "+sha3" with GCC 13 or later, which adds the extension to the build
target. Before GCC 13, the SHA-512 intrinsics are themselves compiled for
Armv8.2-A, so keep "arch=armv8.2-a+sha3" there.

Link: https://github.com/Mbed-TLS/mbedtls/pull/10986
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Julius Bairaktaris <julius@bairaktaris.de>
---
--- a/library/sha512.c
+++ b/library/sha512.c
@@ -91,7 +91,12 @@
 #          error "A more recent GCC is required for MBEDTLS_SHA512_USE_A64_CRYPTO_*"
 #        else
 #          pragma GCC push_options
-#          pragma GCC target ("arch=armv8.2-a+sha3")
+/* Before GCC 13, the SHA-512 intrinsics require Armv8.2-A. */
+#          if __GNUC__ < 13
+#            pragma GCC target ("arch=armv8.2-a+sha3")
+#          else
+#            pragma GCC target ("+sha3")
+#          endif
 #          define MBEDTLS_POP_TARGET_PRAGMA
 #        endif
 #      else
